# Use object stores

Declare the store on the participant and generate the project:

```trellis
participant "acme.documents@v1" service {
  implements "acme.documents-api@v1";
  store documents {
    purpose "Document objects.";
    ttl_ms 0;
    max_object_bytes 1048576;
    max_total_bytes 104857600;
  }
}
```

Use the resolved `service.store` handle after `TrellisService.connect(...)`; do not construct store bindings in application code.

For example, after connecting and registering the service lifecycle:

```ts
const store = await service.store.documents.open().orThrow();
const entry = await store.get("invoice.pdf").orThrow();
const bytes = await entry.bytes().orThrow();
console.log(bytes.length);
```

Keys are logical object names within this service's resolved store. Store limits
are runtime-enforced. Do not construct a bucket name or grant access by passing
binding metadata to another participant.

For caller uploads or downloads, declare a transfer-capable operation and bind
it to this store in the provider participant. Transfer completion verifies the
exact byte count and SHA-256 digest; an operation response alone is not evidence
that the bytes arrived intact. Prefer streaming bodies for large objects.
